# KSV0125: Restrict container images to trusted registries
# Trivy does not recognize ghcr.io as trusted by default. We use ghcr.io for application images.
# Registry validation is enforced at deployment time via policy/OPA Gatekeeper.
KSV0125

# KSV020, KSV021: runAsUser/runAsGroup > 10000
# OpenShift restricted-v2 SCC assigns namespace-specific UID range (e.g. 1002750000-1002759999).
# Cannot hardcode in template; OpenShift injects at deploy time.
KSV020
KSV021

# KSV030, KSV104: seccompProfile
# OpenShift restricted SCC forbids seccomp: "seccomp may not be set".
KSV030
KSV104

# KSV0013: "Image tag ':latest' used" false-positive on templated image refs.
# The templates take a complete IMAGE_REF: the PR tag for DEV previews and a
# SHA-256 digest for TEST and PROD, so runtime images are never :latest.
KSV0013
KSV-0013

# CVE-2026-3260: OSV currently reports this against Undertow.
#
# Status verified 2026-09-06 (nr-lexis): Red Hat states that the assigning CNA
# marked this CVE Rejected. Source: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2026-3260
#
# Retain this suppression unless a distinct, confirmed Undertow issue needs
# review.
CVE-2026-3260

# CVE-2026-47884 (XsltView path limitation) and CVE-2026-47890 (SSE stream corruption with view
# fragments): Spring Framework 6.2.19, as managed by Spring Boot 3.5.16.
#
# The fix is only in Spring Framework 7.0.9+ (Spring Boot 4); 6.2.19 is the newest 6.2.x on Maven
# Central. Neither is reachable here: the backend is a JSON REST API with no XsltView, XSLT
# templates, view resolvers, SseEmitter or view-fragment rendering (checked 2026-10-23).
#
# Remove these suppressions with the Spring Boot 4 upgrade, or sooner if the backend adds XSLT
# views or Server-Sent Events.
CVE-2026-47884
CVE-2026-47890
